[#:seon.task{:name "a-config-read-walks-the-whole-registry"
             :kind :function
             :intent "dial-attributes (and required-dial-attributes) walk every form in the projection's registry on every config/effective call; a trivial agent form reads config three times on fresh database values, 1.9 ms each under load (0.97 ms quiet). Both are functions of the projection alone: keep the answer on the projection's own holder (schema/projection-cache-value; 0.0008 ms on a hit, same answer, the carried projection is identical across commits). Patch: tmp/perf-eval-overhead-opus/patches/config-dial-attributes-memo.patch."
             :must-read #{seon.config/dial-attributes seon.config/effective seon.schema/projection-cache-value}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/perf-eval-overhead-2026-09-26.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "compute-concurrency-dial-has-no-executor"
             :kind :function
             :intent "After d2604ede9 removed the launcher's compute half, :seon.config.flow.compute/concurrency is read only by seon.config's status display and its available-processors default; nothing executes with it. Retire it as 13387dc38 retired its sibling queue-depth, or name the executor that consumes it. The process root's :compute executor (resources/seon/operator/runtime.clj:17-22, availableProcessors platform threads) is likewise unused (active 0, 2026-09-27); test agents (option B) name it as the JVM-wide CPU bound for test bodies."
             :evidence #{"docs/prds/agent-platform/plan/lane-b3-errors-tasks-dials.md"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/test-agents-concurrency-2026-09-27.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "no-provider-cannot-be-lifted-per-agent"
             :kind :schema
             :intent ":seon.config.ai/no-provider is [:= true] and per-agent: an agent overlay can set it but never lift it, so with the cluster's no-provider on (default's standing setting) a branch agent cannot be pointed at a local stub provider without retracting the cluster config row on its branch (what repl-dogfood 2026-09-27 had to do). Make the dial a boolean whose overlay value wins, or document the branch-row route as the entrance."
             :must-read #{seon.config/effective seon.ai/agent-overlay}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/repl-dogfood-2026-09-27.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "an-agent-branch-forked-before-a-new-required-dial-refuses-every-eval-request"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Root applied two new required dials to default's cluster config at 2026-10-08T07:02 (:seon.config.db/store-cache-size, :seon.config.operator/heap-max-bytes). Every agent branch forked before then holds the old config row, so effective-in (src/seon/config.clj:942-975) answers :seon.config/error and every MCP eval request of that agent, SCI and JVM, fails with only the fixed message: agent cards-recording, occurrences 6352f423d616, fb31f3805860, 2455649eb488 (signature dca1c074e22a). Root's own eval requests work. Two defects: a dial added on main never reaches existing branches (CLAUDE.md: a new dial exists at its first read), and the MCP reply drops the error's :seon.error/data, which names the missing dials, so the agent cannot act on it."
             :must-read #{seon.config/effective seon.config/required-dial-attributes seon.mcp/call}
             :evidence #{"docs/seon/schedule/cards/README-recording.md"}}]
